<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>PR Reviewer Metrics — <%= h(meta[:repo]) %></title>
  <style>
<%= inline_css %>
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="app">
    <!-- Table of Contents Sidebar -->
    <nav class="toc">
      <ul class="toc__list">
        <li><a href="#hero" class="active">Overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="#watch">Things to Watch</a></li>
        <li><a href="#breakdown">Reviewer Breakdown</a></li>
        <li><a href="#concentration">Concentration</a></li>
        <li><a href="#scatter">Approval vs Depth</a></li>
        <li><a href="#depth">Review Depth</a></li>
        <li><a href="#response">Response Times</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cross-team">Cross-Team</a></li>
        <li><a href="#ratio">Review/Author Ratio</a></li>
        <li><a href="#methodology">Methodology</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <main class="main">
      <!-- Hero / Page Header -->
      <header class="hero" id="hero">
        <h1 class="hero__title">PR Reviewer Metrics</h1>
        <p class="hero__meta">
          <span class="mono"><%= h(meta[:repo]) %></span>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <%= h(meta[:period_start]) %> – <%= h(meta[:period_end]) %>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <%= meta[:total_reviewers] %> reviewers
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <%= meta[:total_reviews] %> reviews
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <%= meta[:total_prs] %> PRs
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- KPI Strip -->
      <div class="kpi-strip">
        <div class="kpi">
          <div class="kpi__lbl">Total Reviews</div>
          <div class="kpi__val"><%= meta[:total_reviews] %></div>
          <div class="kpi__sub">across <%= meta[:total_prs] %> PRs</div>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi">
          <div class="kpi__lbl">Median Response</div>
          <div class="kpi__val"><%= format_hours(meta[:response_initial_median]) %></div>
          <div class="kpi__sub">initial review pickup</div>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi<%= meta[:bus_factor] && meta[:bus_factor] <= 3 ? ' kpi--warn' : '' %>">
          <div class="kpi__lbl">Bus Factor</div>
          <div class="kpi__val"><%= meta[:bus_factor] || '—' %></div>
          <div class="kpi__sub">reviewers cover 50%</div>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi<%= meta[:gini] && meta[:gini] >= 0.5 ? ' kpi--warn' : '' %>">
          <div class="kpi__lbl">Gini Coefficient</div>
          <div class="kpi__val"><%= meta[:gini]&.round(2) || '—' %></div>
          <div class="kpi__sub"><%= meta[:health] %></div>
        </div>

        <%- single_review_pct = meta[:pr_distribution]&.find { |d| d[:bucket] == '1 review' }&.dig(:pct) -%>
        <div class="kpi">
          <div class="kpi__lbl">Single-Review PRs</div>
          <div class="kpi__val"><%= single_review_pct ? "#{single_review_pct.round(0)}%" : '—' %></div>
          <div class="kpi__sub">merged with 1 review</div>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi kpi--good">
          <div class="kpi__lbl">Changes-Req Follow-Through</div>
          <div class="kpi__val"><%= meta[:review_effectiveness_overall] ? "#{meta[:review_effectiveness_overall].round(0)}%" : '—' %></div>
          <div class="kpi__sub"><%= meta[:changes_requested_followed_by_commit] %>/<%= meta[:changes_requested_total] %> led to commits</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Things to Watch -->
      <section class="section" id="watch">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">01</span>Things to Watch</h2></div>
        <%- if watch_list.empty? -%>
        <p class="muted">No significant issues detected.</p>
        <%- else -%>
        <div class="watchlist">
          <%- watch_list.each do |item| -%>
          <div class="watch <%= severity_class(item[:severity]) %>">
            <div class="watch__sev"><%= item[:severity].to_s.upcase %></div>
            <div class="watch__content">
              <div class="watch__title"><%= h(item[:title]) %></div>
              <div class="watch__text"><%= h(item[:body]) %></div>
              <%- if item[:refs] && !item[:refs].empty? -%>
              <div class="watch__refs">
                <%- item[:refs].each do |ref| -%>
                <a href="#r-<%= h(ref) %>" class="ref-chip"><%= h(ref) %></a>
                <%- end -%>
              </div>
              <%- end -%>
            </div>
          </div>
          <%- end -%>
        </div>
        <%- end -%>
      </section>

      <!-- Reviewer Breakdown - Master Table -->
      <section class="section" id="breakdown">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">02</span>Reviewer Breakdown</h2></div>

        <div class="filters-bar">
          <input type="text" class="search-input" placeholder="Search reviewers...">
          <label class="filter-checkbox">
            <input type="checkbox" id="flagged-only"> Flagged only
          </label>
          <label class="filter-checkbox">
            <input type="checkbox" id="hide-bots" checked> Hide bots
          </label>
          <span class="filter-count"><%= reviewers.length %> of <%= reviewers.length %></span>
        </div>

        <table class="master-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="col-caret"></th>
              <th class="col-name">Reviewer</th>
              <th class="col-volume" data-sort-key="total">Volume <button class="sort-btn">↓</button></th>
              <th class="col-mix">Mix</th>
              <th class="col-approval" data-sort-key="approval">Approval% <button class="sort-btn">↕</button></th>
              <th class="col-depth" data-sort-key="depth">Depth% <button class="sort-btn">↕</button></th>
              <th class="col-response" data-sort-key="response">Response <button class="sort-btn">↕</button></th>
              <th class="col-delta" data-sort-key="delta">Re-review Δ <button class="sort-btn">↕</button></th>
              <th class="col-ratio" data-sort-key="ratio">Rev/Auth <button class="sort-btn">↕</button></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <%- max_volume = reviewers.map { |r| r[:total] }.max || 1 -%>
            <%- approval_range = reviewers.map { |r| r[:approval_pct] }.compact -%>
            <%- approval_min = approval_range.min || 0 -%>
            <%- approval_max = approval_range.max || 100 -%>
            <%- depth_range = reviewers.map { |r| r[:depth_pct] }.compact -%>
            <%- depth_min = depth_range.min || 0 -%>
            <%- depth_max = depth_range.max || 100 -%>
            <%- response_range = reviewers.map { |r| r[:response_initial] }.compact -%>
            <%- response_min = response_range.min || 0 -%>
            <%- response_max = response_range.max || 10 -%>
            <%- delta_range = reviewers.map { |r| r[:response_delta] }.compact -%>
            <%- delta_min = delta_range.min || -5 -%>
            <%- delta_max = delta_range.max || 5 -%>

            <%- reviewers.each do |r| -%>
            <tr id="r-<%= h(r[:name]) %>"
                data-row
                data-name="<%= h(r[:name]) %>"
                data-total="<%= r[:total] %>"
                data-approval="<%= r[:approval_pct] %>"
                data-depth="<%= r[:depth_pct] %>"
                data-response="<%= r[:response_initial] %>"
                data-delta="<%= r[:response_delta] %>"
                data-ratio="<%= r[:ratio] %>"
                data-flagged="<%= r[:flagged] %>"
                data-bot="<%= r[:bot] %>"
                <%= r[:bot] ? 'hidden' : '' %>>
              <td class="col-caret">▸</td>
              <td class="col-name">
                <span class="reviewer-name"><%= h(r[:name]) %></span>
                <%- if r[:bot] -%><span class="bot-tag">bot</span><%- end -%>
                <%- if r[:badges].any? -%>
                <span class="badges">
                  <%- r[:badges].each do |badge| -%>
                    <%- info = badge_info(badge) -%>
                    <span class="<%= info[:class] %>"><%= info[:label] %></span>
                  <%- end -%>
                </span>
                <%- end -%>
              </td>
              <td class="col-volume">
                <div class="databar">
                  <div class="databar__fill" style="width: <%= (r[:total].to_f / max_volume * 100).round(1) %>%; background: var(--accent);"></div>
                  <span class="databar__label"><%= r[:total] %></span>
                </div>
              </td>
              <td class="col-mix">
                <%- mix_total = r[:approved] + r[:changes_requested] + r[:commented] -%>
                <%- if mix_total > 0 -%>
                <div class="stackbar" title="Approved: <%= r[:approved] %> · Changes Req: <%= r[:changes_requested] %> · Commented: <%= r[:commented] %>">
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= (r[:approved].to_f / mix_total * 100).round(1) %>%; background: var(--good);"></div>
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= (r[:changes_requested].to_f / mix_total * 100).round(1) %>%; background: var(--warn);"></div>
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= (r[:commented].to_f / mix_total * 100).round(1) %>%; background: var(--ink-50);"></div>
                </div>
                <%- else -%>
                <span class="muted">—</span>
                <%- end -%>
              </td>
              <td class="col-approval" style="background: <%= heatmap(r[:approval_pct], min: approval_min, max: approval_max) %>">
                <%= r[:approval_pct] ? "#{r[:approval_pct].round(1)}%" : '—' %>
                <%- if r[:approval_pct] && r[:approval_pct] > 95 && r[:actionable] >= 5 -%><span class="star">★</span><%- end -%>
              </td>
              <td class="col-depth" style="background: <%= heatmap(r[:depth_pct], min: depth_min, max: depth_max, invert: true) %>">
                <%= r[:depth_pct] ? "#{r[:depth_pct].round(1)}%" : '—' %>
              </td>
              <td class="col-response" style="background: <%= heatmap(r[:response_initial], min: response_min, max: response_max) %>">
                <%= format_hours(r[:response_initial]) %>
              </td>
              <td class="col-delta" style="background: <%= heatmap(r[:response_delta], min: delta_min, max: delta_max) %>">
                <%= format_delta(r[:response_delta]) %>
              </td>
              <td class="col-ratio">
                <%= r[:ratio] ? "#{r[:ratio]}%" : '—' %>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <!-- Expanded row (hidden by default) -->
            <tr class="exp-row" hidden>
              <td colspan="9">
                <div class="exp-content">
                  <div class="exp-grid">
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Approved</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:approved] %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Changes Req.</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:changes_requested] %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Commented</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:commented] %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Actionable</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:actionable] %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Minimal</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:minimal] || 0 %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Brief</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:brief] || 0 %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Substantive</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:substantive] || 0 %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Share</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:share_pct].round(1) %>%</div>
                    </div>
                    <%- if r[:cross_team_same] || r[:cross_team_cross] -%>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Same Team</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:cross_team_same] || 0 %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">Cross Team</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:cross_team_cross] || 0 %></div>
                    </div>
                    <%- end -%>
                    <%- if r[:chg_req_rate] -%>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">CR Follow-Through</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:chg_req_rate].round(0) %>%</div>
                    </div>
                    <%- end -%>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">PRs Reviewed</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:prs_reviewed] %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="exp-stat">
                      <div class="exp-stat__label">PRs Authored</div>
                      <div class="exp-stat__value"><%= r[:prs_authored] %></div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <%- end -%>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- Concentration & Bus Factor -->
      <section class="section" id="concentration">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">03</span>Review Concentration</h2></div>
        <div class="concentration-layout">
          <div class="concentration-main">
            <!-- Share Tiles -->
            <div class="sharetiles">
              <%- share_tiles_data.each do |tile| -%>
              <div class="sharetiles__tile" style="width: <%= tile[:pct].round(2) %>%; background: <%= tile[:color] %>;" title="<%= h(tile[:name]) %>: <%= tile[:total] %> reviews (<%= tile[:pct].round(1) %>%)">
                <%- if tile[:pct] > 4 -%><span class="sharetiles__lbl"><%= h(tile[:name]) %></span><%- end -%>
              </div>
              <%- end -%>
            </div>

            <!-- Lorenz Curve -->
            <svg width="100%" viewBox="0 0 320 150" class="lorenz">
              <line x1="8" y1="132" x2="272" y2="8" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-dasharray="2 3" />
              <path d="<%= lorenz_curve_path %>" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" />
              <line x1="8" y1="132" x2="272" y2="132" stroke="var(--ink-50)" />
              <line x1="8" y1="8" x2="8" y2="132" stroke="var(--ink-50)" />
              <text x="8" y="145" font-size="8" fill="var(--ink-60)">0%</text>
              <text x="272" y="145" font-size="8" fill="var(--ink-60)" text-anchor="end">100% reviewers</text>
              <text x="10" y="16" font-size="8" fill="var(--ink-60)">% reviews</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <aside class="concentration-aside">
            <h3 class="aside__title">Reviews per PR</h3>
            <div class="distbar">
              <%- pr_dist = meta[:pr_distribution] || [] -%>
              <%- dist_max = pr_dist.map { |d| d[:prs] }.max || 1 -%>
              <%- pr_dist.each do |d| -%>
              <div class="distbar__row">
                <div class="distbar__lbl"><%= d[:bucket] %></div>
                <div class="distbar__track">
                  <div class="distbar__fill" style="width: <%= (d[:prs].to_f / dist_max * 100).round(1) %>%"></div>
                  <span class="distbar__num"><%= d[:prs] %> PRs · <%= d[:pct].round(1) %>%</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <%- end -%>
            </div>

            <dl class="stats-list">
              <dt>Bus Factor</dt><dd><%= meta[:bus_factor] || '—' %></dd>
              <dt>Gini</dt><dd><%= meta[:gini]&.round(2) || '—' %></dd>
              <dt>Top Reviewer</dt><dd><%= meta[:top_share] ? "#{meta[:top_share].round(1)}%" : '—' %></dd>
              <dt>Top 3</dt><dd><%= meta[:top_3_share] ? "#{meta[:top_3_share].round(1)}%" : '—' %></dd>
              <dt>Median/PR</dt><dd><%= meta[:median_reviews_per_pr] || '—' %></dd>
              <dt>Mean/PR</dt><dd><%= meta[:mean_reviews_per_pr]&.round(2) || '—' %></dd>
            </dl>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Approval vs Depth Scatter Plot -->
      <section class="section" id="scatter">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">04</span>Approval Rate vs Review Depth</h2></div>
        <%- scatter = scatter_data -%>
        <%- max_vol = scatter.map { |r| r[:total] }.max || 1 -%>
        <div class="scatter-wrap">
          <svg width="100%" viewBox="0 0 680 360" class="scatter">
            <!-- Rubber-stamp zone shading -->
            <rect x="<%= 36 + (95.0/100) * (560 - 72) %>" y="36" width="<%= (5.0/100) * (560 - 72) %>" height="<%= (85.0/100) * (360 - 72) %>" fill="oklch(0.95 0.06 30)" opacity="0.45" />
            <text x="<%= 36 + (95.0/100) * (560 - 72) + 14 %>" y="180" font-size="8" fill="oklch(0.45 0.13 30)" font-weight="600" transform="rotate(-90 <%= 36 + (95.0/100) * (560 - 72) + 14 %> 180)">RUBBER-STAMP ZONE</text>

            <!-- Gridlines -->
            <%- [0, 25, 50, 75, 100].each do |v| -%>
              <%- x = 36 + (v.to_f/100) * (560 - 72) -%>
              <%- y = 360 - 36 - (v.to_f/100) * (360 - 72) -%>
              <line x1="<%= x %>" y1="36" x2="<%= x %>" y2="324" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-dasharray="2 3" />
              <text x="<%= x %>" y="338" font-size="8" fill="var(--ink-60)" text-anchor="middle"><%= v %>%</text>
              <line x1="36" y1="<%= y %>" x2="524" y2="<%= y %>" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-dasharray="2 3" />
              <text x="32" y="<%= y + 3 %>" font-size="8" fill="var(--ink-60)" text-anchor="end"><%= v %>%</text>
            <%- end -%>

            <!-- Axis labels -->
            <text x="280" y="354" font-size="9" fill="var(--ink-70)" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Approval rate →</text>
            <text x="10" y="180" font-size="9" fill="var(--ink-70)" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" transform="rotate(-90 10 180)">Substantive depth %</text>

            <!-- Data points -->
            <%- scatter.each do |r| -%>
              <%- coords = scatter_coords(r[:approval_pct], r[:depth_pct], r[:total], max_vol) -%>
              <%- in_zone = in_rubber_stamp_zone?(r[:approval_pct], r[:depth_pct]) -%>
              <circle cx="<%= coords[:x] %>" cy="<%= coords[:y] %>" r="<%= coords[:r] %>"
                      fill="<%= in_zone ? 'oklch(0.65 0.16 30)' : 'var(--accent)' %>" opacity="0.55" />
              <text x="<%= coords[:x] + coords[:r] + 3 %>" y="<%= coords[:y] + 3 %>" font-size="8" fill="var(--ink)"><%= h(r[:name]) %></text>
            <%- end -%>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Review Depth Table -->
      <section class="section" id="depth">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">05</span>Review Depth</h2></div>
        <table class="compact-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Reviewer</th>
              <th>Depth Distribution</th>
              <th>Substantive%</th>
              <th>Total</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <%- depth_range = depth_reviewers.map { |r| r[:depth_pct] }.compact -%>
            <%- d_min = depth_range.min || 0 -%>
            <%- d_max = depth_range.max || 100 -%>
            <%- depth_reviewers.sort_by { |r| -(r[:depth_pct] || 0) }.each do |r| -%>
              <%- total_depth = (r[:minimal] || 0) + (r[:brief] || 0) + (r[:substantive] || 0) -%>
            <tr>
              <td><%= h(r[:name]) %></td>
              <td>
                <div class="stackbar" title="Minimal: <%= r[:minimal] || 0 %> · Brief: <%= r[:brief] || 0 %> · Substantive: <%= r[:substantive] || 0 %>">
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= total_depth > 0 ? ((r[:minimal] || 0).to_f / total_depth * 100).round(1) : 0 %>%; background: var(--bad);"></div>
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= total_depth > 0 ? ((r[:brief] || 0).to_f / total_depth * 100).round(1) : 0 %>%; background: var(--warn);"></div>
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= total_depth > 0 ? ((r[:substantive] || 0).to_f / total_depth * 100).round(1) : 0 %>%; background: var(--good);"></div>
                </div>
              </td>
              <td style="background: <%= heatmap(r[:depth_pct], min: d_min, max: d_max, invert: true) %>"><%= format_pct(r[:depth_pct]) %></td>
              <td class="mono"><%= total_depth %></td>
            </tr>
            <%- end -%>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- Response Times Table -->
      <section class="section" id="response">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">06</span>Response Times</h2></div>
        <p class="section__sub">Median response time in business hours (weekdays 8am-6pm ET). Excludes reviewers with fewer than 2 data points.</p>
        <table class="compact-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Reviewer</th>
              <th>Initial</th>
              <th>Re-review</th>
              <th>Δ</th>
              <th>Came back</th>
              <th>N</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <%- response_reviewers.sort_by { |r| r[:response_initial] || 999 }.each do |r| -%>
            <tr>
              <td><%= h(r[:name]) %></td>
              <td>
                <div class="databar">
                  <div class="databar__fill" style="width: <%= [((r[:response_initial] || 0) / 10.0 * 100), 100].min.round(1) %>%; background: <%= response_color(r[:response_initial]) %>;"></div>
                  <span class="databar__label"><%= format_hours(r[:response_initial]) %></span>
                </div>
              </td>
              <td class="mono"><%= format_hours(r[:response_re_review]) %></td>
              <td class="mono" style="color: <%= delta_color(r[:response_delta]) %>; font-weight: <%= r[:response_delta] && r[:response_delta].abs > 3 ? '600' : '400' %>"><%= format_delta(r[:response_delta]) %></td>
              <td class="mono" title="Returned after the author pushed, out of the times they were waited on"><%=
                r[:return_rate] ? "#{r[:return_rate]}% (#{r[:rereview_n]}/#{r[:return_waits]})" : '—'
              %></td>
              <td class="mono"><%= r[:response_n] || '—' %></td>
            </tr>
            <%- end -%>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- Cross-Team Participation -->
      <section class="section" id="cross-team">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">07</span>Cross-Team Participation</h2></div>
        <p class="section__sub">Reviews given to PRs from other teams vs the same team. Overall rate: <%= meta[:cross_team][:rate].round(1) %>%</p>
        <table class="compact-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Reviewer</th>
              <th>Same / Cross</th>
              <th>Cross-Team Rate</th>
              <th>Total</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <%- cs_range = cross_team_reviewers.map { |r| r[:cross_team_rate] }.compact -%>
            <%- cs_min = cs_range.min || 0 -%>
            <%- cs_max = cs_range.max || 100 -%>
            <%- cross_team_reviewers.sort_by { |r| -(r[:cross_team_rate] || 0) }.each do |r| -%>
              <%- cs_total = (r[:cross_team_same] || 0) + (r[:cross_team_cross] || 0) -%>
            <tr>
              <td><%= h(r[:name]) %></td>
              <td>
                <div class="stackbar" title="Same: <%= r[:cross_team_same] || 0 %> · Cross: <%= r[:cross_team_cross] || 0 %>">
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= cs_total > 0 ? ((r[:cross_team_same] || 0).to_f / cs_total * 100).round(1) : 0 %>%; background: var(--ink-50);"></div>
                  <div class="stackbar__seg" style="width: <%= cs_total > 0 ? ((r[:cross_team_cross] || 0).to_f / cs_total * 100).round(1) : 0 %>%; background: var(--accent);"></div>
                </div>
              </td>
              <td style="background: <%= heatmap(r[:cross_team_rate], min: cs_min, max: cs_max, neutral: true) %>"><%= format_pct(r[:cross_team_rate]) %></td>
              <td class="mono"><%= cs_total %></td>
            </tr>
            <%- end -%>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- Review/Author Ratio -->
      <section class="section" id="ratio">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">08</span>Review / Author Ratio</h2></div>
        <p class="section__sub">PRs reviewed vs PRs authored. 100% = reviewing as many as you author.</p>
        <table class="compact-table sortable-table" id="ratio-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th data-sort-key="name">Person <span class="sort-btn">↕</span></th>
              <th data-sort-key="reviewed">Reviewed <span class="sort-btn">↕</span></th>
              <th data-sort-key="authored">Authored <span class="sort-btn">↕</span></th>
              <th data-sort-key="ratio">Ratio <span class="sort-btn">↓</span></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <%- max_r = max_ratio -%>
            <%- ratio_reviewers.sort_by { |r| -(r[:ratio] || -1) }.each do |r| -%>
            <tr data-row data-name="<%= h(r[:name]) %>" data-reviewed="<%= r[:prs_reviewed] %>" data-authored="<%= r[:prs_authored] %>" data-ratio="<%= r[:ratio] || '' %>">
              <td><%= h(r[:name]) %></td>
              <td class="mono"><%= r[:prs_reviewed] %></td>
              <td class="mono"><%= r[:prs_authored] %></td>
              <td style="background: <%= ratio_heatmap(r[:ratio]) %>">
                <%- if r[:ratio] -%>
                <div class="ratio-bar">
                  <div class="ratio-bar__fill" style="width: <%= [(r[:ratio].to_f / max_r * 100), 100].min.round(1) %>%; background: <%= ratio_bar_color(r[:ratio]) %>;"></div>
                  <div class="ratio-bar__tick" style="left: <%= (100.0 / max_r * 100).round(1) %>%"></div>
                  <span class="ratio-bar__label"><%= r[:ratio] %>%</span>
                </div>
                <%- else -%>
                <span class="muted">—</span>
                <%- end -%>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <%- end -%>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- Methodology -->
      <section class="section" id="methodology">
        <div class="section__hd"><h2><span class="num">09</span>Methodology</h2></div>
        <div class="methodology">
          <p><strong>Actionable reviews</strong> are those with a state of APPROVED or CHANGES_REQUESTED. COMMENTED-only reviews are tracked but excluded from approval rate calculations.</p>

          <p><strong>Reviewer badges</strong> highlight patterns: <strong>★ rubber-stamp</strong> = &gt;95% approval rate on 5+ reviews; <strong>shallow</strong> = &gt;50% minimal-depth reviews on 5+ reviews; <strong>load-bearing</strong> = reviews 150%+ more PRs than they author (carrying review load); <strong>under-contributing</strong> = reviews &lt;50% as many PRs as they author with 5+ authored (not pulling review weight).</p>

          <p><strong>Review depth</strong> is categorized by comment length: Minimal (&lt;10 chars), Brief (10-99 chars), Substantive (100+ chars). Depth% is the proportion of substantive reviews.</p>

          <p><strong>Response times</strong> are measured in business hours (weekdays 8am-6pm ET) from review request to first review submission.</p>
          <p><strong>Re-review</strong> is the median time to come back to a pull request you held &mdash; you requested changes, or commented without approving, and the author then pushed. The clock starts at <em>their push</em>, not at your review, so time the author spent working is not counted against the reviewer. <strong>Came back</strong> is how often they returned at all. Not returning is not automatically a problem: someone else may have approved, or the comment may not have been blocking. <strong>&Delta;</strong> compares re-review time with initial response time.</p>

          <p><strong>Bus factor</strong> is the minimum number of reviewers who together account for 50% of all reviews. <strong>Gini coefficient</strong> measures inequality (0 = perfectly equal, 1 = one person does everything).</p>

          <p><strong>Cross-team rate</strong> is the percentage of reviews given to PRs authored by someone on a different team, excluding reviews where either side has no known team.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </main>
  </div>

  <script>
<%= inline_js %>
  </script>
</body>
</html>
